## Other material and existing rights

This grant covers the listed project material, not the entire repository or the software
packages it imports, downloads or invokes. Unlisted material receives no new permission
from this decision. Any existing separate license or written permission continues to
apply according to its own scope; rights already granted for earlier copies are preserved.
Applicable mandatory rights and GitHub's platform permissions are not restricted here.

In particular, this grant does not cover `DataAnalyticsPy/`, `HTML5 Scripts/`,
`cv-local-generator/core/`, `cv-local-generator/data/`, `cv-local-generator/jobs/`,
`assets/`, personal documents, operational inputs, generated reports or exports.
The CV implementation and its listed technical guide can be reused under MIT; that does
not grant permission to reuse the personal or third-party material processed by it.

The existing `assets/AEKR-BANNER-LICENSE.txt` retains its separate scope and notices.
No trademark, logo, endorsement or personal-data permission is created by this grant.
Preserve the applicable notices for any separately licensed material you distribute.

For the component inventory and decision history, see [docs/licensing.md](docs/licensing.md).
That document explains this index and does not expand its list. Adding a new file to the
repository does not automatically add it to this MIT grant; update the index explicitly
when the rights holder elects to include it.
